OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Uncomment if using OpenAI directly:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
Feature 1 — Voice Chat with Memory
You speak into the mic, the character hears you, thinks, and talks back — in their own voice. Every character has a distinct ElevenLabs voice and a distinct personality baked into their system prompt. The memory system stores your last 12 messages and a long-term summary per user-character pair, so the character always knows who you are and what you've talked about. It's not a chatbot — it's a relationship that carries over every session.

Feature 2 — Story Characters with Zep Graph Memory
Princess Elena and Yodha are characters from PocketFM's own original stories — and they know exactly what happened to them. We ingest the full story transcript into a Zep knowledge graph on startup; when you ask a question, the 8 most relevant plot facts are retrieved and injected into the prompt. Without this, the character would hallucinate its own backstory. With it, Elena can tell you precisely what happened the night The Haven was attacked — because she was there.

Feature 3 — Debate Arena
Pick 2 to 5 characters, give them a topic, and watch a live structured debate stream — each character argues in their own voice, with a moderator managing turns and closing each round. Every turn is streamed as a Server-Sent Event containing the argument text and base64 audio, so you hear each character speak in real time. We anchor each character's round-1 position and inject it into every later prompt, so Victor never suddenly agrees with Lily just because the context drifted. No consumer AI product has shipped a multi-character, multi-voice, real-time debate format like this.

Feature 4 — Character Marketplace
Anyone can build an AI character — personality, voice, backstory, knowledge domain — list it on the Marketplace, and earn revenue from every interaction. A Marketplace character is the same object used in voice chat and the debate arena, so it works across every feature from the moment it's published. The licensing model is flexible: per-message, subscription, or one-time. The Debate Arena acts as the discovery engine — users find new characters by watching them argue, then pay to chat with them directly.

Feature 5 — The Case Engine (AI Detective Game)
Every time you press New Case, an LLM writes a fresh murder mystery — new victim, new killer, new motive, new rooms — and an AI-painted scene is generated for each room in parallel. You explore by hovering hotspots, question suspects in free text, and unlock new rooms by finding clues; the host character narrates everything in their own voice and personality. Swapping the host — Inspector Quill, Bix Marrow, or Madame Corvina — completely changes the tone of the show while the underlying case stays identical. The solution never reaches the browser, the NPCs have real memory and can be pressured into cracking, and the whole thing goes from click to playable in 9 seconds.

